{"id": "wwdc2019-518", "language": "eng", "source": "https://developer.apple.com/videos/play/wwdc2019/518", "wordCount": 1951, "segments": [{"start": 15.0, "text": "Good morning, everyone."}, {"start": 16.0, "text": "My name is Devin."}, {"start": 17.0, "text": "I'm thrilled to be here today"}, {"start": 19.0, "text": "with all of you to tell you"}, {"start": 20.0, "text": "about what's new in WebKit."}, {"start": 23.0, "text": "There's a lot we have to talk about today, so we're going to"}, {"start": 25.0, "text": "dive right in."}, {"start": 26.0, "text": "There are a lot of things that"}, {"start": 27.0, "text": "are new and exciting for the web"}, {"start": 29.0, "text": "platform and for web developers"}, {"start": 30.0, "text": "this year."}, {"start": 32.0, "text": "Today's talk is going to cover a"}, {"start": 33.0, "text": "variety of different topics"}, {"start": 35.0, "text": "ranging from web specific APIs"}, {"start": 38.0, "text": "to new ways that you can provide"}, {"start": 39.0, "text": "a more native experience from"}, {"start": 41.0, "text": "within your web content."}, {"start": 42.0, "text": "We have a lot to discuss, so"}, {"start": 44.0, "text": "we're going to dive right in"}, {"start": 46.0, "text": "starting with Dark Mode."}, {"start": 48.0, "text": "The system Dark Mode was first"}, {"start": 50.0, "text": "introduced in MacOS Mojave."}, {"start": 51.0, "text": "But this year, it also comes to"}, {"start": 54.0, "text": "iOS as part of iOS 13."}, {"start": 57.0, "text": "This means that the desktop"}, {"start": 59.0, "text": "experience and the mobile"}, {"start": 61.0, "text": "experience can now both adapt to"}, {"start": 63.0, "text": "Dark Mode. But don't worry."}, {"start": 65.0, "text": "It, it's not that complicated."}, {"start": 67.0, "text": "It's very easy to have your web"}, {"start": 69.0, "text": "content also adapt to Dark Mode."}, {"start": 71.0, "text": "Let's take a look at it."}, {"start": 73.0, "text": "First, adding a color scheme CSS"}, {"start": 76.0, "text": "property to any root CSS rule"}, {"start": 78.0, "text": "with a value that includes dark"}, {"start": 81.0, "text": "will tell WebKit that the entire"}, {"start": 83.0, "text": "page supports Dark Mode."}, {"start": 85.0, "text": "And when in Dark Mode, the"}, {"start": 86.0, "text": "default text and background"}, {"start": 88.0, "text": "colors, as well as any form"}, {"start": 90.0, "text": "controls, will automatically"}, {"start": 92.0, "text": "update to match the rest of the"}, {"start": 93.0, "text": "darker theme."}, {"start": 94.0, "text": "But as you can see, this won't"}, {"start": 96.0, "text": "do anything for custom styles."}, {"start": 98.0, "text": "So, you'll still need to update"}, {"start": 99.0, "text": "them yourself."}, {"start": 100.0, "text": "The way you can do that is using"}, {"start": 102.0, "text": "a prefers color scheme dark CSS"}, {"start": 104.0, "text": "media query."}, {"start": 106.0, "text": "It behaves just like any other"}, {"start": 108.0, "text": "CSS media query, meaning that"}, {"start": 110.0, "text": "the contained styles only apply"}, {"start": 112.0, "text": "when the system is in Dark Mode."}, {"start": 114.0, "text": "You can use this to change any"}, {"start": 116.0, "text": "other custom styles like CSS"}, {"start": 118.0, "text": "images or other colors to match"}, {"start": 120.0, "text": "the rest of the darker theme on"}, {"start": 121.0, "text": "the page."}, {"start": 122.0, "text": "But for images that are not in"}, {"start": 124.0, "text": "CSS, you can always use the"}, {"start": 126.0, "text": "picture element through HTML."}, {"start": 129.0, "text": "And using the exact same media"}, {"start": 130.0, "text": "query it will cause the two"}, {"start": 132.0, "text": "images to automatically switch"}, {"start": 134.0, "text": "between when the user enables"}, {"start": 136.0, "text": "Dark Mode."}, {"start": 138.0, "text": "It's that simple."}, {"start": 139.0, "text": "And obviously, for any other"}, {"start": 141.0, "text": "content, you can always use the"}, {"start": 143.0, "text": "JavaScript matchMedia API,"}, {"start": 146.0, "text": "again, with the exact same media"}, {"start": 147.0, "text": "query to handle any other"}, {"start": 149.0, "text": "dynamic content."}, {"start": 151.0, "text": "All of these techniques make it"}, {"start": 153.0, "text": "really easy for you to adapt"}, {"start": 155.0, "text": "Dark Mode to support the rest of"}, {"start": 156.0, "text": "your web content."}, {"start": 158.0, "text": "And we can't wait to see your"}, {"start": 159.0, "text": "super cool dark websites."}, {"start": 162.0, "text": "For more information about this,"}, {"start": 164.0, "text": "there's a great post on the"}, {"start": 165.0, "text": "WebKit blog and a great video in"}, {"start": 167.0, "text": "the WWDC App that talks all"}, {"start": 169.0, "text": "about supporting Dark Mode in"}, {"start": 171.0, "text": "web content."}, {"start": 172.0, "text": "Be sure to check it out."}, {"start": 173.0, "text": "And that's a very quick look at"}, {"start": 177.0, "text": "how to support Dark Mode in your"}, {"start": 178.0, "text": "web content."}, {"start": 179.0, "text": "It's very easy."}, {"start": 182.0, "text": "Next, let's talk about a very"}, {"start": 184.0, "text": "simple API that you can use"}, {"start": 186.0, "text": "called Web Share which allows"}, {"start": 187.0, "text": "you to invoke the native share"}, {"start": 189.0, "text": "sheet from within web content."}, {"start": 191.0, "text": "It's standardized and it works"}, {"start": 193.0, "text": "anywhere, whether that be in"}, {"start": 195.0, "text": "Safari or in WK web view in an"}, {"start": 197.0, "text": "app."}, {"start": 198.0, "text": "It's especially great on iOS"}, {"start": 200.0, "text": "this year with all of the"}, {"start": 201.0, "text": "improvements to the native share"}, {"start": 205.0, "text": "sheet. Using it is as simple as calling"}, {"start": 207.0, "text": "navigator.share with the"}, {"start": 208.0, "text": "relevant data."}, {"start": 210.0, "text": "It returns a promise which"}, {"start": 211.0, "text": "resolves if a share action is"}, {"start": 213.0, "text": "completed or rejects if the"}, {"start": 214.0, "text": "share sheet is dismissed."}, {"start": 216.0, "text": "But keep in mind this API"}, {"start": 218.0, "text": "expects to be called in response"}, {"start": 220.0, "text": "to a user gesture like a tap."}, {"start": 223.0, "text": "So, if that's not the case, it"}, {"start": 225.0, "text": "will immediately reject."}, {"start": 227.0, "text": "One of the cool things is that"}, {"start": 228.0, "text": "you can already see the Web"}, {"start": 230.0, "text": "Share API in action as it's been"}, {"start": 232.0, "text": "adopted by some pretty major"}, {"start": 233.0, "text": "websites."}, {"start": 235.0, "text": "A great example of this is"}, {"start": 236.0, "text": "Twitter which also has some"}, {"start": 237.0, "text": "phenomenal support for Dark"}, {"start": 239.0, "text": "Mode."}, {"start": 240.0, "text": "Tapping any of the Share icons"}, {"start": 242.0, "text": "on the page will open the native"}, {"start": 243.0, "text": "share sheet with the title and"}, {"start": 245.0, "text": "link of that tweet."}, {"start": 246.0, "text": "And you can try this out for"}, {"start": 247.0, "text": "yourself in iOS 12.2 or later."}, {"start": 250.0, "text": "And that's the Web Share API."}, {"start": 253.0, "text": "A really simple way to invoke"}, {"start": 255.0, "text": "native functionality from within"}, {"start": 257.0, "text": "your web content."}, {"start": 260.0, "text": "Now, let's move a little bit on"}, {"start": 262.0, "text": "to some new media features."}, {"start": 264.0, "text": "If you're developing a website"}, {"start": 265.0, "text": "that strives to display the"}, {"start": 267.0, "text": "content that is best suited for"}, {"start": 269.0, "text": "the user's device."}, {"start": 270.0, "text": "You can now use the new Media"}, {"start": 272.0, "text": "Capabilities API to determine"}, {"start": 274.0, "text": "whether any video codec is"}, {"start": 275.0, "text": "supported as well as if that"}, {"start": 277.0, "text": "video codec will be fast enough"}, {"start": 279.0, "text": "to knock off any frames or will"}, {"start": 281.0, "text": "be power efficient during"}, {"start": 282.0, "text": "playback."}, {"start": 283.0, "text": "This empowers you to make a more"}, {"start": 285.0, "text": "informed decision about the type"}, {"start": 287.0, "text": "of content you want to present."}, {"start": 290.0, "text": "And speaking of video content,"}, {"start": 292.0, "text": "macOS Catalina and iOS 13 also"}, {"start": 295.0, "text": "bring support for alpha channel"}, {"start": 296.0, "text": "video."}, {"start": 298.0, "text": "Alpha channel video allows for"}, {"start": 300.0, "text": "any HEVC encoded video content"}, {"start": 302.0, "text": "to contain transparent pixels."}, {"start": 304.0, "text": "A very compelling use case of"}, {"start": 306.0, "text": "this is that it allows your"}, {"start": 308.0, "text": "video to seamlessly integrate"}, {"start": 310.0, "text": "with the surrounding content"}, {"start": 311.0, "text": "when the user enables Dark Mode."}, {"start": 314.0, "text": "Instead of making two separate"}, {"start": 315.0, "text": "videos, one for use in Light"}, {"start": 317.0, "text": "Mode and one for use in Dark"}, {"start": 318.0, "text": "Mode, a single video with a"}, {"start": 320.0, "text": "transparent background would"}, {"start": 322.0, "text": "likely work for both."}, {"start": 324.0, "text": "And alpha channel videos can be"}, {"start": 325.0, "text": "used anywhere that videos can be"}, {"start": 327.0, "text": "used today."}, {"start": 328.0, "text": "There's no special syntax,"}, {"start": 329.0, "text": "there's no special MIME type."}, {"start": 331.0, "text": "It just works."}, {"start": 333.0, "text": "But before you use it, you'll"}, {"start": 335.0, "text": "want to make sure that alpha"}, {"start": 336.0, "text": "channel video is available, such"}, {"start": 338.0, "text": "as on older iOS or older macOS,"}, {"start": 340.0, "text": "which you can do by adding an"}, {"start": 342.0, "text": "alpha channel key to the, to"}, {"start": 344.0, "text": "your capabilities object when"}, {"start": 346.0, "text": "using the Media Capabilities"}, {"start": 347.0, "text": "API."}, {"start": 351.0, "text": "If you'd like to know a little"}, {"start": 352.0, "text": "bit more about alpha channel"}, {"start": 353.0, "text": "video, including how to create"}, {"start": 354.0, "text": "those videos on macOS Catalina,"}, {"start": 356.0, "text": "be sure to check out the video"}, {"start": 358.0, "text": "about creating HEVC videos with"}, {"start": 359.0, "text": "alpha."}, {"start": 363.0, "text": "But if instead, you're a web"}, {"start": 364.0, "text": "developer who builds a website"}, {"start": 366.0, "text": "that includes peer-to-peer chat"}, {"start": 368.0, "text": "functionality and you also want"}, {"start": 369.0, "text": "to provide screen capture, you"}, {"start": 371.0, "text": "can now use the getDisplayMedia"}, {"start": 373.0, "text": "API in Safari 13."}, {"start": 375.0, "text": "Calling it will gain return a"}, {"start": 377.0, "text": "promise and immediately prompt"}, {"start": 379.0, "text": "the user for permission to"}, {"start": 380.0, "text": "capture their screen."}, {"start": 382.0, "text": "If that permission is granted,"}, {"start": 384.0, "text": "the promise will return with a"}, {"start": 385.0, "text": "standard media stream of the"}, {"start": 387.0, "text": "space that contains the Safari"}, {"start": 389.0, "text": "window."}, {"start": 390.0, "text": "The returned media stream"}, {"start": 392.0, "text": "behaves just like any other"}, {"start": 393.0, "text": "standard media stream, meaning"}, {"start": 395.0, "text": "that it can be used with WebRTC"}, {"start": 396.0, "text": "to share your screen with"}, {"start": 398.0, "text": "another person."}, {"start": 399.0, "text": "And those are some of the new"}, {"start": 402.0, "text": "media features coming to macOS"}, {"start": 404.0, "text": "Catalina, iOS 13, and Safari 13."}, {"start": 407.0, "text": "Now, we're going to talk a"}, {"start": 410.0, "text": "little bit about a few new tools"}, {"start": 412.0, "text": "that you can use to make your"}, {"start": 414.0, "text": "web content more responsive and"}, {"start": 416.0, "text": "performant on all platforms."}, {"start": 420.0, "text": "As web developers, part of our"}, {"start": 422.0, "text": "job is to make sure that we"}, {"start": 424.0, "text": "provide an experience that"}, {"start": 426.0, "text": "doesn't consume too much battery"}, {"start": 428.0, "text": "or unnecessarily perform"}, {"start": 429.0, "text": "actions."}, {"start": 431.0, "text": "To help you better understand"}, {"start": 433.0, "text": "why those things might be"}, {"start": 434.0, "text": "happening, the Web Inspector has"}, {"start": 436.0, "text": "added a new CPU Timeline."}, {"start": 438.0, "text": "This interface is packed with"}, {"start": 441.0, "text": "actionable information."}, {"start": 442.0, "text": "And we really want you to be"}, {"start": 443.0, "text": "able to use it effectively."}, {"start": 445.0, "text": "So, we've created a post on the"}, {"start": 447.0, "text": "WebKit blog and a video in the"}, {"start": 449.0, "text": "WWDC App all about understanding"}, {"start": 451.0, "text": "CPU usage with Web Inspector."}, {"start": 453.0, "text": "Definitely check it out."}, {"start": 454.0, "text": "It'll do wonders for your"}, {"start": 455.0, "text": "website."}, {"start": 456.0, "text": "And WebDriver is coming to iOS."}, {"start": 461.0, "text": "The standardized test format"}, {"start": 462.0, "text": "from the W3C for automation and"}, {"start": 465.0, "text": "regression testing is available"}, {"start": 467.0, "text": "on all iOS devices running iOS"}, {"start": 468.0, "text": "13."}, {"start": 470.0, "text": "You can use WebDriver to"}, {"start": 471.0, "text": "automate regression testing of"}, {"start": 473.0, "text": "your web content and make sure"}, {"start": 475.0, "text": "that your, all the platforms you"}, {"start": 477.0, "text": "support, whether that be desktop"}, {"start": 479.0, "text": "or mobile, keep working exactly"}, {"start": 481.0, "text": "as you would expect."}, {"start": 483.0, "text": "WebDriver on iOS works much the"}, {"start": 485.0, "text": "same as on macOS."}, {"start": 486.0, "text": "And we have phenomenal"}, {"start": 487.0, "text": "documentation for that on"}, {"start": 489.0, "text": "developer.apple.com."}, {"start": 490.0, "text": "And we have some blog posts"}, {"start": 491.0, "text": "coming soon to talk more about"}, {"start": 493.0, "text": "it."}, {"start": 495.0, "text": "Now, let's change it a little"}, {"start": 496.0, "text": "bit and talk about how to store"}, {"start": 497.0, "text": "structured data from within your"}, {"start": 499.0, "text": "web content."}, {"start": 500.0, "text": "There have been two main ways of"}, {"start": 503.0, "text": "doing this in the past;"}, {"start": 504.0, "text": "IndexedDB and WebSQL."}, {"start": 506.0, "text": "In Safari 13, WebSQL has been"}, {"start": 508.0, "text": "completely removed."}, {"start": 511.0, "text": "All modern web browsers,"}, {"start": 512.0, "text": "including Safari, support"}, {"start": 514.0, "text": "IndexedDB."}, {"start": 515.0, "text": "And over the past year, we've"}, {"start": 517.0, "text": "been hard at work making it more"}, {"start": 518.0, "text": "standards compliant."}, {"start": 520.0, "text": "So, if you haven't already, be"}, {"start": 522.0, "text": "sure to transition to using"}, {"start": 523.0, "text": "IndexedDB as soon as possible."}, {"start": 529.0, "text": "And finally, let's talk about"}, {"start": 530.0, "text": "Apple Pay, the easiest way to"}, {"start": 532.0, "text": "accept payments on the web."}, {"start": 534.0, "text": "We have two main things to talk"}, {"start": 536.0, "text": "about."}, {"start": 537.0, "text": "The first, Apple Pay, is now"}, {"start": 540.0, "text": "fully supported with all of its"}, {"start": 541.0, "text": "capabilities using the Payment"}, {"start": 543.0, "text": "Request API."}, {"start": 545.0, "text": "Bringing the entirety of Apple"}, {"start": 547.0, "text": "Pay JS's private, secure, and"}, {"start": 550.0, "text": "streamlined experience to your"}, {"start": 551.0, "text": "web content in a more"}, {"start": 552.0, "text": "standardized way."}, {"start": 554.0, "text": "We strongly encourage you to"}, {"start": 555.0, "text": "switch to the Payment Request"}, {"start": 556.0, "text": "API as it supports everything"}, {"start": 559.0, "text": "that Apple Pay JS can do and"}, {"start": 560.0, "text": "it's continuing to evolve."}, {"start": 563.0, "text": "For a deeper dive into how to"}, {"start": 564.0, "text": "use the Payment Request API for"}, {"start": 566.0, "text": "Apple Pay, there's going to be a"}, {"start": 567.0, "text": "great post on the WebKit blog"}, {"start": 569.0, "text": "later today that'll do a deep"}, {"start": 571.0, "text": "dive into these new improvements."}, {"start": 573.0, "text": "And second, in iOS 13, you can"}, {"start": 577.0, "text": "now use Apple Pay inside a"}, {"start": 579.0, "text": "WKWebView."}, {"start": 580.0, "text": "Yeah."}, {"start": 586.0, "text": "This means that Apple Pay is now"}, {"start": 587.0, "text": "available in even more apps."}, {"start": 589.0, "text": "But there are a few things to"}, {"start": 590.0, "text": "consider."}, {"start": 592.0, "text": "When a user attempts to make a"}, {"start": 593.0, "text": "purchase through Apple Pay,"}, {"start": 595.0, "text": "there's an expectation that"}, {"start": 596.0, "text": "they're communicating with the"}, {"start": 598.0, "text": "page, not the containing web"}, {"start": 599.0, "text": "browser or app."}, {"start": 601.0, "text": "Nothing should get in between"}, {"start": 604.0, "text": "the user and the webpage during"}, {"start": 606.0, "text": "the transaction or before it's"}, {"start": 608.0, "text": "even started."}, {"start": 609.0, "text": "So, this means there are fewer"}, {"start": 610.0, "text": "restrictions about when you can"}, {"start": 612.0, "text": "use Apple Pay inside the"}, {"start": 613.0, "text": "WKWebView as well as when you"}, {"start": 615.0, "text": "can inject script into a"}, {"start": 617.0, "text": "WKWebView."}, {"start": 618.0, "text": "Here's how it works."}, {"start": 620.0, "text": "If any script has ever been"}, {"start": 622.0, "text": "injected to the current page of"}, {"start": 624.0, "text": "the WKWebView, we will not allow"}, {"start": 626.0, "text": "Apple Pay."}, {"start": 627.0, "text": "If the current page has already"}, {"start": 630.0, "text": "called canMakePayments with an"}, {"start": 632.0, "text": "Apple Pay payment method, we"}, {"start": 634.0, "text": "will not allow any future script"}, {"start": 635.0, "text": "injections."}, {"start": 636.0, "text": "They will be blocked with an"}, {"start": 637.0, "text": "error."}, {"start": 638.0, "text": "But both of these restrictions"}, {"start": 640.0, "text": "are only limited to the current"}, {"start": 642.0, "text": "page."}, {"start": 643.0, "text": "So, any top-level navigation"}, {"start": 644.0, "text": "will cause them to reset."}, {"start": 646.0, "text": "So, what does all of this mean?"}, {"start": 650.0, "text": "If you're a web developer, it's"}, {"start": 652.0, "text": "really important that you call"}, {"start": 654.0, "text": "canMakePayments before you"}, {"start": 656.0, "text": "attempt to show an Apple Pay"}, {"start": 657.0, "text": "button or even start anything"}, {"start": 659.0, "text": "with Apple Pay."}, {"start": 661.0, "text": "This way, your users will never"}, {"start": 663.0, "text": "encounter a situation where an"}, {"start": 664.0, "text": "Apple Pay button is shown and"}, {"start": 666.0, "text": "tapping on it doesn't do"}, {"start": 667.0, "text": "anything because it's been"}, {"start": 668.0, "text": "disabled."}, {"start": 669.0, "text": "And if instead, you're an app"}, {"start": 671.0, "text": "developer, really think about"}, {"start": 674.0, "text": "whether you actually need to"}, {"start": 675.0, "text": "inject script such as through"}, {"start": 677.0, "text": "the WKUserScript API or the"}, {"start": 678.0, "text": "evaluateJavaScript with"}, {"start": 680.0, "text": "completionHandler call."}, {"start": 682.0, "text": "We've seen some examples in the"}, {"start": 683.0, "text": "past of apps injecting script"}, {"start": 686.0, "text": "when there's a WebKit API that"}, {"start": 688.0, "text": "does the exact same thing."}, {"start": 689.0, "text": "There's no reason for that."}, {"start": 691.0, "text": "By injecting script, you could"}, {"start": 693.0, "text": "be preventing the loaded web"}, {"start": 695.0, "text": "content from providing its best"}, {"start": 697.0, "text": "experience."}, {"start": 698.0, "text": "And that's what's new with Apple"}, {"start": 702.0, "text": "Pay."}, {"start": 703.0, "text": "This was a quick look at some of"}, {"start": 705.0, "text": "the great features available"}, {"start": 707.0, "text": "that are new for web developers"}, {"start": 708.0, "text": "this year."}, {"start": 710.0, "text": "You'll also definitely want to"}, {"start": 712.0, "text": "check out Introducing"}, {"start": 713.0, "text": "Desktop-class Browsing on iPad,"}, {"start": 715.0, "text": "which covers how to use some"}, {"start": 717.0, "text": "other new web platform features"}, {"start": 719.0, "text": "like pointer events to really"}, {"start": 720.0, "text": "make your desktop website feel"}, {"start": 723.0, "text": "right at home on iPad."}, {"start": 725.0, "text": "I really hope you've enjoyed"}, {"start": 726.0, "text": "learning about what's new for"}, {"start": 728.0, "text": "web developers."}, {"start": 729.0, "text": "We can't wait to see what"}, {"start": 730.0, "text": "beautiful designs and incredible"}, {"start": 732.0, "text": "experiences you craft with these"}, {"start": 734.0, "text": "new features and tools that are"}, {"start": 735.0, "text": "available to you."}]}